# AI steering and pathfinding
@scenario tutorial_lesson_45
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[stage clear]
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set tutorial_source scripts/tutorial/45_ai_lab.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt open_ai]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Move the green marker. The ochre follower uses a chase behavior and the same collision map. Compare whether it can follow through the gap.
@label lab
> Run the follower demo -> demo
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Practice exercise -> practice
> Review question -> check
@label demo
# region open_ai
[jes push scripts/scenes/ai_lab.jes label compare]
# endregion
@label compare
[set tutorial_source scripts/scenes/ai_lab.jes]
[set tutorial_excerpt ai]
ginger: Set aggroRange to 96 and change the initial positions. The follower should only activate when the target is close enough.
[jump lab]
@label return_hub
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[if !tutorial_done_45]
[flag tutorial_done_45]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_9]
[end]

@label practice
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Set aggroRange to 96. What should you test?
> Only the original outline color. -> practice_hint
> Approach the follower from outside the range, then cross inside. -> practice_result
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label practice_hint
ginger: The AI compares the distance to its configured range and handles movement toward the target.
[jump practice]
@label practice_result
ginger: The AI compares the distance to its configured range and handles movement toward the target.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Review question -> check
> Try the lab again -> start
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: What controls when the follower activates?
> Its aggro range and target distance. -> correct
> The image format of the follower. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
ginger: The AI compares the distance to its configured range and handles movement toward the target.
[jump check]
@label correct
ginger: The AI compares the distance to its configured range and handles movement toward the target.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
